# 4. Governance Scope and Security Boundary

This boundary is mandatory:

> The MCP Gateway is authoritative for capabilities routed through it. It does not automatically govern native runtime capabilities such as built-in shell execution, filesystem access, browser capabilities, or other runtime-native tools.

Therefore the real security model is:

```text
Agent
├── Native runtime capabilities
│      └── Claude/Codex/native runtime controls
│
└── Shared governed capabilities
       ↓
   MCP Gateway
       ↓
 Central governance
```

Where practical, sensitive shared capabilities should be routed through the Gateway and direct bypass paths removed after safe verification.

Do not claim the Gateway governs a capability unless that capability actually passes through the Gateway or an equivalent enforceable control.

Do not accept prompt instructions such as "the agent must not use this tool" as proof of enforcement. A prohibited Gateway-routed operation must be rejected outside the model.

