# 10. Canonical Configuration vs Runtime State

Keep **desired state** separate from **operational state**.

```text
.agents-hub
├── policies
├── roles
├── capabilities
├── schemas
└── registries
     ↓
canonical desired state

MCP Gateway runtime
├── active connections
├── health/state
├── request state
├── token/session material where required
├── runtime cache
└── audit events
     ↓
operational state
```

Do not use `.agents-hub` or Git as a runtime database.

The Gateway may load/compile/cache canonical configuration, but operational noise, request state, tokens, health data, logs, and ephemeral state must not be written back into canonical governance files merely because they are convenient.

Runtime state must never silently become a competing source of governance truth.

